# Agent temporary files

When creating files for the agent's own use (probes, dumps, scratch scripts, HTML captures, exploratory notes, one-off debug helpers) that should not ship as production code:

- Place them under `temp/` at the project root (create the folder if needed).
- Do **not** write them next to production modules (e.g. `source/scraper/`, app packages, or repo root).
- Prefer names that make the purpose obvious (e.g. `temp/fetch_noresults.py`, `temp/NoResults.html`).

Production scripts, configs, tests the team owns, and intentional project artifacts still go in their normal locations.